  "lifecycleStatus": "awaiting-approval",
  "title": "Custom Undo/Redo Across Embedded Code Regions",
  "branch": "feature/prompt-undo-across-regions",
  "summary": "Give the prompt editor a single PromptUndoManager that owns Ctrl\u002BZ/Ctrl\u002BY across host text and every embedded AvalonEdit region, restoring the exact selection and caret from a {serializedText, caretOffset, anchorOffset} snapshot over the flat GetPlainText()/ToFencedText() serialization. caretOffset and anchorOffset are absolute offsets in that one flat coordinate space, so a single selection may straddle the host\u2194region boundary and must still capture and restore with correct span and direction. Native RichTextBox undo and per-region AvalonEdit undo are suppressed so exactly one authority exists; edits coalesce and history clears on send.",
  "tasks": [
    {
      "taskId": "PROMPTUNDO-20261015-001",
      "title": "Decide the single-authority prompt undo architecture",
      "description": "Establish and record the authoritative design for prompt undo/redo before any wiring begins.\n\n## Observable outcome\n\nA new entry in \u0060.squad/decisions.md\u0060 plus a design contract that tasks 002-006 consume, so the implementation has one agreed model rather than per-task reinterpretation. No production behavior changes in this task.\n\n## Decisions to fix\n\n- A single \u0060PromptUndoManager\u0060 owns Ctrl\u002BZ/Ctrl\u002BY for the entire prompt \u0060RichTextBox\u0060, including when focus is inside an embedded region\u0027s AvalonEdit control.\n- The undo unit is a snapshot \u0060{serializedText, caretOffset, anchorOffset}\u0060 captured over the flat \u0060GetPlainText()\u0060/\u0060ToFencedText()\u0060 serialization.\n- **Absolute flat coordinate space.** \u0060caretOffset\u0060 and \u0060anchorOffset\u0060 are absolute offsets measured from the start of the single flat serialized prompt, a coordinate space that spans host text AND every embedded region\u0027s fenced span. Because both endpoints live in one space, a single selection may straddle the host\u2194region boundary in either orientation (anchor in host / caret in region, or anchor in region / caret in host).\n- **Selection-direction rule.** \u0060anchorOffset\u0060 and \u0060caretOffset\u0060 are stored separately so a forward selection (anchor before caret) and a backward selection (caret before anchor) each restore with the active caret on the correct end; the manager\u0027s authoritative range is the absolute [min,max] span plus the stored direction.\n- Single-authority routing suppresses native \u0060RichTextBox\u0060 undo and each region\u0027s AvalonEdit per-region undo stack.\n- Rapid consecutive edits coalesce into one undo entry; undo/redo history clears when the prompt is sent.\n\n## Consumers\n\nTasks 002 (snapshot engine), 003 (routing), 004 (coalescing/clear), 005 (tests), and 006 (review fixture) all build on this contract.",
