    {
      "taskId": "PROMPTUNDO-20261015-002",
      "title": "Capture and restore prompt snapshots across the region seam",
      "description": "Implement \u0060PromptUndoManager\u0060 snapshot capture and apply over the flat serialization, grounded in \u0060EmbeddedCodeRegionManager.ResolveCaretPointerAfterRebuild\u0060/\u0060GetCaretOffset\u0060, \u0060RichTextBoxExtensions.GetPlainText\u0060 and its fenced-offset mapping (\u0060GetCharOffset\u0060/\u0060GetTextPointerAt\u0060), and the \u0060IRegionCodeEditor\u0060/\u0060AvalonEditRegionEditor\u0060 seam (\u0060CaretOffset\u0060, \u0060SelectionStart\u0060, \u0060SelectionLength\u0060).\n\n## Observable outcome\n\nCapturing a snapshot then applying it rebuilds the prompt document from \u0060serializedText\u0060 and restores the exact selection \u2014 same span, same caret end \u2014 for host-text selections, collapsed carets, selections entirely inside one region, and selections that straddle the host\u2194region boundary. This capture/apply engine is consumed by the Ctrl\u002BZ/Ctrl\u002BY routing in task 003 and the coalescing/clear path in task 004.\n\n## Boundary-straddling selections (first-class)\n\n\u0060caretOffset\u0060 and \u0060anchorOffset\u0060 are absolute offsets in the one flat serialized-prompt coordinate space that spans host text and every embedded region\u0027s fenced span. A single selection may straddle the host\u2194region boundary in either orientation: anchor in host text with caret inside a region, OR anchor inside a region with caret in host text. Capture and restore must resolve a selection whose anchor and caret resolve to DIFFERENT surfaces \u2014 one host \u0060TextPointer\u0060, one in-region AvalonEdit offset \u2014 into one coherent WPF-level selection spanning the \u0060BlockUIContainer\u0060 boundary, preserving direction (which endpoint is the moving caret).\n\nBecause \u0060GetCharOffset\u0060 treats a region\u0027s fenced span as one indivisible block, an absolute offset that lands inside a region must additionally resolve to that specific region plus its internal AvalonEdit local offset. The content base is the absolute offset of the first content character after the opener line: for a fenced span serialized as \u0060{fence}{lang}\\n{content}\\n{fence}\u0060, content local offset L maps to absolute (spanStart \u002B fenceLen \u002B langLen \u002B 1 \u002B L).\n\nIf a WPF \u0060RichTextBox\u0060 selection cannot natively render a single visible highlight spanning a \u0060BlockUIContainer\u0060 plus its nested AvalonEdit control, the authoritative selection in \u0060PromptUndoManager\u0060 remains the absolute [min,max] range with stored direction, and the visible selection must reflect that range as faithfully as the control composition allows. The straddle case must never be silently dropped.",
      "dependsOn": [
        "PROMPTUNDO-20261015-001"
      ],
      "priority": "critical",
      "status": "complete",
      "commit": "6d449071dae4d8d9b22ba354f755c1bf91c71c35",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-15T14:37:02.7386677+00:00",
