      "reviewActivity": [
        {
          "kind": "manual-correction",
          "summary": "Fixed live prompt undo/redo failing to restore the pre-edit selection (commit 5e893c11 on feature/prompt-undo-across-regions). Root cause: snapshots were captured only post-edit (PromptTextBox_TextChanged / OnEmbeddedRegionContentEdited), so Undo landed on an entry predating the replaced selection, and for the first edit after a simulation load it restored the baseline captured with caretIndex:0 \u2014 sending the caret to offset 0 (the user\u0027s \u0027jumps to the front of the prompt\u0027 on selection-replace). Lyra Morn added guarded pre-edit selection capture (host RichTextBox SelectionChanged \u002B a new IRegionCodeEditor TextChanging pre-edit notification forwarded from AvalonEditRegionEditor/EmbeddedCodeRegionBlock) that refreshes the current PromptUndoHistory entry\u0027s caret/anchor in place via a new PromptUndoManager.RefreshSelection \u2014 without adding history or truncating redo \u2014 so Undo restores the exact forward/backward/collapsed/in-region selection with direction; also removed the host-selection collapse (CaretPosition set after Selection.Select) in RestoreResolvedSelection. Added 20 history-level regression tests (EmbeddedCodeRegionPreEditUndoTests.cs) and strengthened EmbeddedCodeRegionFlatOffsetUndoTests to assert actual restored host selections; filtered suite 271 passed / 0 failed, build green (benign NU1701 only). Assessed item 6: partial mouse selection straddling the host\u2194region boundary is inherent to the two-control composition (each region is an atomic BlockUIContainer; Shift\u002BArrow is not a workaround) and remains unsupported \u2014 recommend deferring the undo-straddle-selection-direction GATE-001 check via a bounded plan revision. Plan remains paused at GATE-001 for the user to re-verify checks 1\u20135 in Developer \u2192 Simulation \u2192 \u0027Prompt Undo Review\u0027.",
          "recordedAt": "2026-10-15T22:52:43.6167231+00:00"
        },
        {
          "kind": "manual-correction",
          "summary": "Fixed the in-region undo off-by-one (GATE check undo-restores-in-region-selection): selecting a whole word inside a region (e.g. \u0027add\u0027), replacing it, then Ctrl\u002BZ restored only \u0027ad\u0027. Root cause: EmbeddedCodeRegionBlock.GetContentSelectionLocal() assumed the physical caret is the selection\u0027s moving endpoint, but AvalonEdit whole-word selection can leave the caret inside the highlighted span, so capture recorded a one-char-short selection even though SelectionLength was correct; neither notification timing nor content-base math was at fault. Lyra Morn changed capture to read AvalonEdit\u0027s directed Selection.StartPosition/EndPosition (via GetSelectionOffsets) and preserve native direction on restore, and added 8 history-level regression cases (forward/backward, interior/endpoint caret, native PerformTextInput \u002B redirected input, live pre-edit capture, full-word Undo, Redo) in EmbeddedCodeRegionPreEditUndoTests that reproduced \u0027add\u0027-\u003E\u0027ad\u0027 before the fix. Committed 334c8bac on feature/prompt-undo-across-regions; filtered suite 279 passed / 0 failed (baseline 271), build green (benign NU1701 only). Item 5 (undo-straddle-selection-direction): deeper feasibility pass confirms partial host\u003C-\u003Eregion straddle selection cannot be created via the current two-control composition (host RichTextBox treats each region as an atomic BlockUIContainer; nested AvalonEdit owns its own mouse capture). The snapshot capture/resolution layer already supports arbitrary straddle endpoints and Step 5 round-trip tests cover resolution, but RestoreResolvedSelection projects straddles onto atomic host boundaries and no UI mechanism can produce a partial-region endpoint without a shared cross-control selection model (Shift\u002BClick/Shift\u002BArrow bridge) \u2014 a substantial, medium-to-high-risk effort. No gesture hack was added. Recommend deferring the undo-straddle-selection-direction GATE check via a bounded plan revision and scheduling shared-selection work as separate follow-up. Plan remains paused at GATE-001 for the user to re-verify the in-region check (and items 1-3/redo) in Developer -\u003E Simulation -\u003E \u0027Prompt Undo Review\u0027.",
          "recordedAt": "2026-10-16T00:55:44.9191192+00:00"
        }
      ],
